.com/news/microsoft-q4-fy2026-azure-100-billion-ai-spending))  \n\n## Where to see *today’s* freshest Azure AI changes (release notes vs. blog posts)\n- **Azure Updates** (filter to *Azure AI Foundry*, *Azure OpenAI Service*, *Azure AI Search*, etc.) is the most direct “shipping/preview/retirement” feed. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- **Microsoft Foundry developer blog** is a good feed for platform-level shipping recaps (Build-to-monthly roundups). ([devblogs.microsoft.com](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/foundry/))  \n\nIf you tell me which part of “Azure AI” you care about (**Azure OpenAI**, **Azure AI Foundry/Foundry Agent Service**, **Azure AI Search**, **Document Intelligence**, **Content Safety**, etc.), I can narrow this to the **most recent 5–10 concrete items** (GA/preview/retirements) that matter for that specific service area."}

